From: kilix-multiplexer maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Guard terminal dimensions and allocation failures
Origin: kilix-multiplexer commit 13dad84d7cf5093c9ac690da3c40c3b038b2197a

This records exactly the existing libvterm changes introduced by the commit
above. Reject dimensions whose signed cell indexing would overflow, check
allocation sizes, and handle allocation failures before initializing buffers.
The original pinned upstream SHA256SUMS remain unchanged.

